                {
                  "id": "candidate-02",
                  "version": "agent.2",
                  "label": "Zero-allocation fused chain replayed via CUDA Graph",
                  "title": "Zero-allocation fused chain replayed via CUDA Graph",
                  "hypothesis": "For an 8192-element fp32 elementwise chain the runtime is launch-bound, not compute-bound. Removing all allocations via out= plus collapsing the 4 launches into one graph replay should cut p50 substantially below the 11.168us reached by the in-place-chain approach.",
                  "change": "run(inputs) computes relu(x*1.25 + y*0.75 - 0.125) by (1) capturing the four ops (torch.mul(...,out=), add_(y, alpha=0.75), sub_(0.125), relu_()) into a torch.cuda.CUDAGraph on a side stream during the first call for a given shape, then replaying it; (2) on any pointer mismatch or capture exception, running the same zero-allocation eager chain into torch.empty_like(x). Coefficients and op order mirror reference() exactly (x*1.25, then +y*0.75, then -0.125) so numerical divergence stays near fp32 epsilon, far inside the 1e-5 atol/rtol. Input tensors are never mutated.",
                  "files": "run.py",
                  "status": "弱候选参考",
                  "classification": "reference",
